      "claims": [
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "TimestampSigner records signing time and can expire signatures; its unsign method may raise SignatureExpired when unsigning fails because the signature is expired.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "c41b8dfb-ae0c-5e37-9aaf-b7381a5bc594"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "On sign, TimestampSigner appends a base64-encoded timestamp from get_timestamp() (int(time.time())) to the value before computing the signature.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "c41b8dfb-ae0c-5e37-9aaf-b7381a5bc594"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "During unsign, when max_age is not None, age is computed as get_timestamp() minus the embedded timestamp ts_int; if age > max_age, SignatureExpired is raised with message indicating age exceeds max_age seconds, payload value, and date_signed from timestamp_to_datetime(ts_int).",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "23a3f312-33a1-5397-9401-8431754f08e3",
            "c41b8dfb-ae0c-5e37-9aaf-b7381a5bc594"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "During unsign with max_age set, if age < 0, SignatureExpired is also raised (signature timestamp appears in the future relative to current time).",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "23a3f312-33a1-5397-9401-8431754f08e3",
            "3e93cc5e-4260-51ea-9418-68cbcdf56a98"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "SignatureExpired is raised when a signature timestamp is older than max_age and is a subclass of BadTimeSignature.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "1b0ce5a6-9dbf-5f15-a1f7-5dce134101ec"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "BadTimeSignature (and thus SignatureExpired) exposes date_signed on the exception when the signature expired, as a timezone-aware datetime.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "298b0109-72a0-5d41-874d-dad5397e78df",
            "979ceafb-b275-5002-a657-2a88ce68bb7f"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "TimedSerializer.loads accepts max_age in seconds; if provided it ensures the signature is not older than that duration via the signer's unsign, and raises SignatureExpired when outdated; SignatureExpired is re-raised without trying other signers.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "95476751-e373-52a5-846d-9d5fa227776d"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "observed",
          "text": "TimestampSigner.validate returns True only if unsign(signed_value, max_age=max_age) succeeds; BadSignature is caught and yields False (SignatureExpired is not caught here and would propagate).",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "da7e4dc1-1e3e-586f-830f-03c21a142af6",
            "c41b8dfb-ae0c-5e37-9aaf-b7381a5bc594"
          ]
        },
        {
          "kind": "inference",
          "text": "Expiration is enforced at verification time by comparing elapsed seconds since the embedded sign-time to max_age; signatures do not auto-invalidate without calling unsign/loads/validate with max_age.",
          "evidence_ids": [
            "23a3f312-33a1-5397-9401-8431754f08e3",
            "95476751-e373-52a5-846d-9d5fa227776d"
          ]
        }
      ],
